Some more tinkering on my part has turned up another bug (which does not
seem to have been reported previously, in opposition to the water
walking "new" bug previously posted about, although one of the #nethack
denizens claims to have seen this before).  These relate to the way
stoning and sliming death messages are being handled, and results in
two rather obtuse messages:

* Being slimed while stoning produces "petrified by a green slime".
* Being stoned on one of the last few turns before dying to sliming
  produces e.g. "turned to slime by a cockatrice egg".

Some more interactions can result into a plain "turned into green slime"
(being stoned and fixing this while sliming is taking place) or "killed
by petrification" (being lifesaved from sliming while stoning), but
these are well-formed death messages and I do not consider them to be
problematic.

